  "content": {
    "id": "p7-q4-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "4",
    "prompt": "Given that $\\sin\\theta=-\\frac{1}{3}$ and $\\theta$ is in Quadrant IV, find each of the following:",
    "layout": "grid",
    "columns": 3,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p7-q4-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "$\\sin 2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{9}$",
          "worked": "In Quadrant IV, $\\cos\\theta>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\cos\\theta&=\\sqrt{1-\\left(-\\frac13\\right)^2}\\\\\\cos\\theta&=\\frac{2\\sqrt2}{3}\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}\\sin2\\theta&=2\\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta\\\\\\sin2\\theta&=2\\left(-\\frac13\\right)\\left(\\frac{2\\sqrt2}{3}\\right)\\\\\\sin2\\theta&=-\\frac{4\\sqrt2}{9}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 45
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q4-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "$\\cos 2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\frac79$",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\cos2\\theta&=1-2\\sin^2\\theta\\\\\\cos2\\theta&=1-2\\left(-\\frac13\\right)^2\\\\\\cos2\\theta&=\\frac79\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 30
      },
      {
        "id": "p7-q4-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "$\\tan 2\\theta$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$-\\frac{4\\sqrt2}{7}$",
          "worked": "In Quadrant IV, $\\cos\\theta=\\frac{2\\sqrt2}{3}$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{-1/3}{2\\sqrt2/3}\\\\\\tan\\theta&=-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt2}\\\\\\tan2\\theta&=\\frac{2\\tan\\theta}{1-\\tan^2\\theta}\\\\\\tan2\\theta&=\\frac{-1/\\sqrt2}{1-1/8}\\\\\\tan2\\theta&=-\\frac{4\\sqrt2}{7}\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 48
      }
    ]
  },
